# sdist contents. setuptools already adds pyproject.toml, README.md, LICENSE*, the tes package and
# its package-data; this adds the documents the README points readers to, which a distro packager
# needs next to the code (licence-adjacent privacy and data-source statements, change history,
# the security contact).
include CHANGELOG.md PRIVACY.md DATA_SOURCES.md SECURITY.md

# tests/ is NOT shipped: several tests read repo-level files the sdist does not contain
# (scripts/, corpus/schema.sql, data/corpus_pool/*.jsonl, ...), so from an sdist they fail on
# "file not found", not on a defect. A test suite that cannot pass where it ships is not a
# deliverable; the suite runs from a git checkout (see CONTRIBUTING.md).
prune tests
